  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Tuesday 15 January 1907, for the places of Wm. White, R. G. Lonsdale, W. Miller, George Lunn, jun., and Joshua McNeice. Four of those nominated withdrew, so seven went to the poll. Declared about 9.15 p.m.; \"There were no spoiled papers.\" The electorate is not given; the Lurgan Mail of 20 January 1912 (p. 5) gives 775 as the number who polled. No party labels printed."
